course: dictionary
lesson: 12528
title: Desperately: one word, three shades
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Desperately is an adverb. It tells you how someone does something, or how much or how badly. Its meaning changes with the sentence, so the context clues matter. «She desperately wanted a puppy.» The clue is wanted: she wanted it so much that it hurts, so desperately means very much.
explain: «He swam desperately for the shore.» The clues are swam and for the shore. He is in trouble and has little hope, so desperately means in a wild way, with all his strength. In «They were desperately poor», the word means extremely, very badly. Try each meaning in the sentence and see which one fits.
explain: Ask yourself: is someone in great need, great fear or great effort? In «Mole runs desperately through the Wild Wood», Mole is frightened and hurrying with all his might. The clues show the feeling, so you can work out the meaning.
fact: Desperately is an adverb, so it tells how, how much or how badly something happens.
fact: «Desperately» can mean very much, so much it hurts: «She desperately wanted a puppy.»
fact: «Desperately» can mean in a wild way, when things are bad and there is little hope: «He swam desperately for the shore.»
fact: «Desperately» can also mean extremely or very badly: «They were desperately poor.»
fact: In news and stories, desperately shows great need, fear or effort: «People desperately need help after the flood.»
exercise: «The little girl desperately wanted a bike for her birthday.» What does desperately mean here? | *Very much, so much it hurts | In a wild way, with no hope at all | Only just | Quietly and slowly
exercise: «He swam desperately for the shore as the boat sank.» What does desperately show about the swimmer? | *Great effort and little hope | He was very tall | A calm, relaxed swim on a sunny day | Boredom and sleepiness
exercise: «The village was desperately cold in winter.» What does desperately mean? | Happily, with a smile | Very quietly | *Extremely, very badly | Only just, barely
test: «Mole runs desperately through the Wild Wood.» Which meaning fits best? | Slowly and calmly | Extremely cold | *In a wild, frightened hurry | Very much, so much it hurts
test: «People desperately need help after the flood.» What does desperately show? | Quiet reading | A happy party | *Great need | Cold weather
exam: The fox «desperately dug a hole to hide» from the hunters. What does desperately mean? | *In a wild way, with little hope of escape | Very slowly and carefully | Only just, barely | Very happy and calm
